description:
FILED s449 (Fable, round-7 companion-leg attribution).  Found because uni/ had not been in a companion leg since s444: the snapshot row (26/32) was blessed at the s444-era 528-file scan, and every tree from f95fa97 on measures 18/5 with one aborted form.  Bisected across round 5's merge order: GOOD at c42cc8a (s444), GOOD at d0d32b6/82dc86a/c3b3eaf/8600556 (M, L, J, I tips), BROKEN at f95fa97 (K's range) -- agent K's #463 glob-value parse family owns the window.

MINIMAL REPRO (5 lines, all-ASCII -- k4 in the s449 scratch; the utf8 names in uni/parser.t are irrelevant):

    my $a = "plainname";
    *$a = sub { 5 };
    print "p1\n";
    *$a = \10;
    print "p2=", ${*$a{SCALAR}} // "u", "\n";
        perl: p1 / p2=10
        PCL:  the whole top-level form dies "Can't use an undefined value as a symbol reference" (no output at all)

THE DISCRIMINATING PAIR: the same file WITHOUT the `${*$a{SCALAR}}` read runs clean (k5) -- the dying expression is the glob-ELEMENT read `*$a{SCALAR}` (or the `${...}` deref of its result), NOT the two glob assignments.  Two candidate shapes for the fix session to separate: (a) `*$a{SCALAR}` returns undef although the slot was just assigned (a slot-read bug in the #463-era glob-value path), and then (b) the `${ undef }` deref reports the SYMBOL-reference message where perl's would be a SCALAR-reference one -- (a) is the bug, (b) just mislabels it.

COST: t/uni/parser.t 26 ok / 32 notok (58 produced, no abort) -> 18/5 (23 produced, one aborted form holding 35 rows).  The snapshot row is spliced with this task as cause (s449).

BAR: the k4 repro + k5 inverse vs perl; uni/parser.t back to >= 26/32 with the aborted form gone; op/gv.t's glob-elem rows re-checked (same family); cl/ change so the op/+uni/ companion legs.

DONE s451w (commit d79a8a5).  ROOT CAUSE was NOT (a) or (b) as filed: it is PPI's ->symbol answering %a for the $a in *$a{SCALAR} -- its cast set is qw{ $ @ % }, missing * (ppi-upstream-bugs.md 27, Bug 27 in ppi-bug-report.t, canary in misc-fixes-02.t).  The rename pass skips a token whose ->symbol is a different variable, so *$a{SCALAR} kept reading the never-assigned PACKAGE global.  The SAME wrong answer reached the expression compiler for a MAGIC symbol: *$_{HASH} emitted (p-dynamic-typeglob (p-gethash %_ "HASH")) -- a SILENT WRONG live in core Carp.pm, five sites.  Fixed where all ~40 ->symbol consumers pass through: Pl::Parser::_brace_glob_slot_symbol wraps the Symbol's TEXT in braces in _ppi_parse's repair group, so the reparse gives *{$x}{SLOT} -- emission-identical.  NEGATIVE: 8 *$Config{sizesize} is multiplication and PPI lexes that * as an Operator, not a Cast (verified after call/subscript/hash elem/string/number/paren).  uni/parser.t 18/5 with one aborted form -> 28/30, 58 rows, no abort (two rows ABOVE the pre-regression 26/32); op/gv.t, op/filetest.t, op/stat.t at snapshot.  Emission A/B 1036 files: exactly two diffs, uni/parser.t and Carp.pm.  Generation v2-380, three artifacts regenerated; pack.t 5636/89 = baseline.  Guard Pl/t/glob-slot-operand-01.t (6 rows, 1.1 s; inverse-run: rows 1-2 fail without the pass).
